all right so we've talked about git and  github but how do you actually get  things done on github how do you go  about creating a project and introducing  change this is the github workflow there  are five basic steps that will walk you  through how to introduce change so let's  say you're working on a project that  project would be stored in a github  repository and all of the code that was  in production is on a branch called  master now that's important we don't  ever want to make changes directly onto  master so the first thing we do is  create another branch when you create a  branch it's creating what feels like an  exact replica of master so you have a  safe sandbox to make changes without  affecting anything that's in production  after you create your branch you make  some commits now commits are sort of  like making changes whenever you make a  set of changes you make a commit and it  stores all of those changes by taking a  snapshot of your repository your project  at that point in time so if this circle  is a commit you could make one tiny  change or you can make a few get lets  you choose once you've made some commits  to introduce your changes you'd open up  a pull request on github comm in this  pull request you're comparing the branch  you made with another branch like master  it gives you an opportunity to look at  the differences between those two  branches and show other people the  differences as well once you do that and  they see the changes then you can  collaborate on them they might give you  a thumbs up and say it looks great or  they might have some critiques and  suggestions and that's good that's the  point right  so you've opened the pull requests  you've gotten some feedback maybe even  made some more changes and made some  more commits on that branch once you've  reached a consensus that it's in a good  place you merge when you merge you're  taking the branch you created and the  commits on that branch and putting them  back into master so all of those  snapshots are in the production branch  so just remember the five basic steps  for the github workflow create a branch  make some commits open up a pull request  collaborate and merge your bridge  you
 

